.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it was not used.) After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15139, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MYpKFL9YFkj7eSAJJhyRgi", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15139, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MYpKFL9YFkj7eSAJJhyRgi", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18562, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and passing health checks again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n1. **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. I rolled it back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. I skipped v2.3.1-rc because it had only been healthy in staging, never in production.\n2. **Check after rollback:** all three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 is open and describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Y8DJuybAwwWgnQWQMM51qd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LsG